 "sentences": [
  {
   "first": 0,
   "last": 8,
   "start": 4.88,
   "end": 13.3,
   "text": "near, rocky, orbit, powerful Alireza is visiting an observatory."
  },
  {
   "first": 9,
   "last": 13,
   "start": 14.04,
   "end": 14.92,
   "text": "He is talking to Ms."
  },
  {
   "first": 14,
   "last": 17,
   "start": 15.16,
   "end": 16.62,
   "text": "Tabesh who works there."
  },
  {
   "first": 18,
   "last": 24,
   "start": 19.56,
   "end": 21.1,
   "text": "Ms.Tabesh: Are you interested in the planets?"
  },
  {
   "first": 25,
   "last": 26,
   "start": 21.66,
   "end": 21.98,
   "text": "Alireza: Yes!"
  },
  {
   "first": 27,
   "last": 39,
   "start": 22.16,
   "end": 26.34,
   "text": "They are really interesting for me, but I don't know much about them."
  },
  {
   "first": 40,
   "last": 49,
   "start": 26.34,
   "end": 29.86,
   "text": "Ms.Tabesh: Planets are really amazing but not so much alike."
  },
  {
   "first": 50,
   "last": 56,
   "start": 30.44,
   "end": 31.88,
   "text": "Do you know how they are different?"
  },
  {
   "first": 57,
   "last": 58,
   "start": null,
   "end": null,
   "text": "Alireza: Umm..."
  },
  {
   "first": 59,
   "last": 68,
   "start": 33.3,
   "end": 36.18,
   "text": "I know they go around the Sun in different orbits."
  },
  {
   "first": 69,
   "last": 71,
   "start": 36.86,
   "end": 37.5,
   "text": "Ms.Tabesh: That's right."
  },
  {
   "first": 72,
   "last": 78,
   "start": 38.04,
   "end": 40.54,
   "text": "They have different colors and sizes, too."
  },
  {
   "first": 79,
   "last": 94,
   "start": 41.02,
   "end": 47.06,
   "text": "Some are rocky like Mars, some have rings like Saturn and some have moons like Uranus."
  },
  {
   "first": 95,
   "last": 97,
   "start": 47.44,
   "end": 48.02,
   "text": "Alireza: How wonderful!"
  },
  {
   "first": 98,
   "last": 104,
   "start": 48.66,
   "end": 50.4,
   "text": "Can we see them without a telescope?"
  },
  {
   "first": 105,
   "last": 125,
   "start": 51.0,
   "end": 60.38,
   "text": "Ms.Tabesh: Yeah..., we can see the planets nearer to us without a telescope, such as Mercury, Venus, Mars, Jupiter and Saturn."
  },
  {
   "first": 126,
   "last": 135,
   "start": 60.8,
   "end": 65.1,
   "text": "We can see Uranus and Neptune only with powerful telescopes."
  },
  {
   "first": 136,
   "last": 144,
   "start": 65.74,
   "end": 68.42,
   "text": "Alireza: And which planet is the largest of all?"
  },
  {
   "first": 145,
   "last": 150,
   "start": 69.02,
   "end": 70.88,
   "text": "Ms.Tabesh: Jupiter is the largest one."
  },
  {
   "first": 151,
   "last": 156,
   "start": 71.08,
   "end": 72.96,
   "text": "It has more than sixty moons."
  },
  {
   "first": 157,
   "last": 163,
   "start": 73.46,
   "end": 74.52,
   "text": "Do you want to look at it?"
  },
  {
   "first": 164,
   "last": 168,
   "start": 74.98,
   "end": 76.16,
   "text": "Alireza: I really like that."
  },
  {
   "first": 169,
   "last": 173,
   "start": null,
   "end": null,
   "text": "Answer the following questions orally."
  },
  {
   "first": 174,
   "last": 174,
   "start": null,
   "end": null,
   "text": "1."
  },
  {
   "first": 175,
   "last": 179,
   "start": null,
   "end": null,
   "text": "How are the planets different?"
  },
  {
   "first": 180,
   "last": 180,
   "start": null,
   "end": null,
   "text": "2."
  },
  {
   "first": 181,
   "last": 188,
   "start": null,
   "end": null,
   "text": "Can we see all planets without a telescope?"
  },
  {
   "first": 189,
   "last": 189,
   "start": null,
   "end": null,
   "text": "3."
  },
  {
   "first": 190,
   "last": 199,
   "start": null,
   "end": null,
   "text": "Do you know the names of the planets in Persian?"
  }
 ],
